STORIES_LOAD("mk",{"mk1":{"passage":[[1,21,39]],"intro":[{"sc":"synagogue","n":"On the Sabbath, Jesus went into the synagogue in Capernaum and began to teach. The people were amazed, because He taught them as one who had authority, not like the teachers of the law."},{"sc":"synagogue","n":"Suddenly a man possessed by an evil spirit cried out. Jesus said sternly, \"Be quiet! Come out of him!\" The spirit shook the man violently and came out with a shriek. \"What is this? He even gives orders to evil spirits, and they obey Him!\""},{"sc":"hut","n":"As soon as they left the synagogue, they went to Simon Peter's house. Peter's mother-in-law was in bed with a fever. Jesus took her hand and helped her up. The fever left her, and she began to serve them."},{"sc":"townnight","n":"That evening after sunset, the whole town gathered at the door! People brought all who were sick, and Jesus healed many."},{"sc":"hillcountry","n":"Very early the next morning, while it was still dark, Jesus got up, left the house and went off to a solitary place, where He prayed."},{"sc":"hillcountry","w":"bpeter","e":"worried","t":"Everyone is looking for You!"},{"sc":"hillcountry","w":"bjesus","e":"smile","t":"Let's go somewhere else, to the nearby villages, so I can preach there also. That's why I have come."},{"sc":"synagogue","n":"🔎 Did you know? Mark uses the word 'immediately' more than 40 times! His Gospel moves fast, like an action story."}],"lesson":{"title":"Busy, but never too busy to pray","text":"Jesus had an exhausting day: teaching, healing, a whole town at the door. And the very next morning, before anyone else was awake, He went to pray. Leaders who serve others need time alone with God, especially when they're busy."},"order":["Jesus teaches with authority","He drives out an evil spirit","He heals Peter's mother-in-law","The whole town gathers at the door","Early next morning, He prays alone","He moves on to preach in other villages"],"quiz":[{"q":"What did Jesus do very early the next morning?","o":["Went to a solitary place to pray","Slept in","Went fishing","Ate breakfast"],"why":"Mark 1:35."},{"q":"Whose mother-in-law did Jesus heal?","o":["Peter's","John's","Matthew's","Andrew's only"],"why":"Mark 1:30."},{"q":"What was amazing about Jesus' teaching?","o":["He taught with authority","It was very long","It was loud","It was in Greek"],"why":"Mark 1:22."}],"words":["CAPERNAUM","AUTHORITY","FEVER","PRAYED","EARLY","HEALED"]},"mk2":{"passage":[[1,40,45]],"intro":[{"sc":"hillcountry","n":"A man with leprosy came to Jesus. Leprosy was a terrible skin disease. People with it had to live outside the towns, alone, and shout 'Unclean! Unclean!' so no one would come near them. Nobody had touched him in years."},{"sc":"hillcountry","w":"bleperm","e":"worried","t":"If You are willing, You can make me clean."},{"sc":"hillcountry","n":"Jesus was filled with compassion. He reached out His hand and touched the man!"},{"sc":"hillcountry","w":"bjesus","e":"smile","t":"I am willing. Be clean!"},{"sc":"hillcountry","n":"Immediately the leprosy left him, and he was clean."},{"sc":"hillcountry","n":"Jesus told him to show himself to the priest, as the law of Moses required, so he could be welcomed back into the community. But the man was so excited, he told everyone!"},{"sc":"hillcountry","n":"🔎 Did you know? Under the law, touching a person with leprosy would make you 'unclean'. But when Jesus touched the man, the opposite happened: Jesus didn't become unclean; the man became clean!"}],"lesson":{"title":"Touch the untouchable","text":"Jesus could have healed the man with a word. Instead, He touched him, the first touch the man had felt in years. Jesus' compassion reached the people everyone else avoided. Leaders notice the lonely and left-out, and reach out to them."},"order":["A man with leprosy comes to Jesus","Nobody would touch him","\"If You are willing...\"","Jesus touches him","\"I am willing. Be clean!\"","He is healed immediately"],"quiz":[{"q":"What did the man say to Jesus?","o":["If You are willing, You can make me clean","Go away","Give me money","I'm fine"],"why":"Mark 1:40."},{"q":"What did Jesus do before healing him?","o":["Touched him","Ran away","Shouted","Prayed all night"],"why":"Mark 1:41."},{"q":"What happened when Jesus touched the man?","o":["The man became clean","Jesus got leprosy","Nothing","The man ran away"],"why":"Mark 1:42."}],"words":["LEPROSY","TOUCH","WILLING","CLEAN","COMPASSION","HEALED"]},"mk3":{"passage":[[2,1,12]],"intro":[{"sc":"flatroof","n":"Jesus was back in Capernaum, teaching in a house. So many people came that there was no room left, not even outside the door!"},{"sc":"flatroof","n":"Four men arrived, carrying their friend who was paralysed, on a mat. But they couldn't get anywhere near Jesus because of the crowd."},{"sc":"flatroof","w":"bfriend4","e":"big","t":"The roof! Let's go up on the roof!"},{"sc":"flatroof","n":"Houses had flat roofs made of beams, branches and dried mud, with stairs outside. The four friends climbed up, dug a hole right through the roof above Jesus, and lowered their friend down on his mat!"},{"sc":"flatroof","w":"bjesus","e":"smile","t":"Son, your sins are forgiven."},{"sc":"flatroof","n":"Some teachers of the law thought, \"Who can forgive sins but God alone?\" Jesus knew what they were thinking. \"Which is easier: to say 'Your sins are forgiven', or 'Get up and walk'? So you may know that the Son of Man has authority to forgive sins...\" He said to the man, \"Get up, take your mat and go home.\""},{"sc":"flatroof","n":"The man got up, picked up his mat and walked out in full view of them all! Everyone was amazed and praised God: \"We've never seen anything like this!\""}],"lesson":{"title":"Friends who carry you to Jesus","text":"The paralysed man couldn't get to Jesus on his own. His four friends carried him, wouldn't give up, and dug through a roof! Mark says Jesus saw 'their faith'. Be the kind of friend who brings others to Jesus, whatever it takes."},"order":["The house is packed","Four friends carry a paralysed man","They can't get in","They dig through the roof","\"Your sins are forgiven\"","The man takes his mat and walks"],"quiz":[{"q":"How did the friends get the man to Jesus?","o":["Lowered him through a hole in the roof","Through the window","Through the back door","They waited outside"],"why":"Mark 2:4."},{"q":"What did Jesus say first to the man?","o":["Your sins are forgiven","Go home","Stand up","Why are you here?"],"why":"Mark 2:5."},{"q":"Whose faith did Jesus see?","o":["Their faith, the friends'","Nobody's","Only the teachers'","Only His own"],"why":"Mark 2:5."}],"words":["ROOF","FRIENDS","MAT","FORGIVEN","WALK","FAITH"]},"mk4":{"passage":[[2,27,28],[3,1,6]],"intro":[{"sc":"synagogue","n":"The Sabbath was God's gift of a weekly rest day. But some religious leaders had added hundreds of extra rules about it, and were watching Jesus closely."},{"sc":"synagogue","w":"bjesus","e":"smile","t":"The Sabbath was made for people, not people for the Sabbath."},{"sc":"synagogue","n":"Another Sabbath, in the synagogue, there was a man with a shrivelled hand. The leaders watched to see if Jesus would heal him, so they could accuse Him."},{"sc":"synagogue","w":"bjesus","e":"stern","t":"Stand up in front of everyone. Which is lawful on the Sabbath: to do good or to do evil, to save life or to kill?"},{"sc":"synagogue","n":"But they stayed silent. Jesus looked around at them in anger, deeply distressed at their stubborn hearts."},{"sc":"synagogue","w":"bjesus","e":"smile","t":"Stretch out your hand."},{"sc":"synagogue","n":"The man stretched it out, and his hand was completely restored! But the Pharisees went out and began to plot with Herod's supporters how they might kill Jesus."}],"lesson":{"title":"People matter more than rules","text":"God's rules are good, and they're given to help people. These leaders cared more about their extra rules than about a man's hand, and Jesus was angry about their hard hearts. Leaders never use rules as an excuse not to help someone."},"order":["The Sabbath was made for people","A man has a shrivelled hand","The leaders watch Jesus","\"Is it right to do good on the Sabbath?\"","\"Stretch out your hand\"","The hand is restored"],"quiz":[{"q":"What did Jesus say the Sabbath was made for?","o":["People","Rules","Kings","Animals"],"why":"Mark 2:27."},{"q":"What was wrong with the man's hand?","o":["It was shrivelled","It was broken","It was cut","Nothing"],"why":"Mark 3:1."},{"q":"How did Jesus feel about the leaders' hard hearts?","o":["Angry and deeply distressed","Happy","Bored","Scared"],"why":"Mark 3:5."}],"words":["SABBATH","HAND","STRETCH","RESTORED","PEOPLE","RULES"]},"mk5":{"passage":[[3,13,19]],"intro":[{"sc":"mountside","n":"Jesus went up on a mountainside and called to Him those He wanted, and they came to Him."},{"sc":"mountside","n":"He appointed twelve, \"that they might be WITH Him, and that He might send them out to preach\"."},{"sc":"mountside","n":"The twelve were: Simon, whom He named Peter; James and his brother John, whom He nicknamed 'Boanerges', which means 'Sons of Thunder'!; Andrew, Philip, Bartholomew, Matthew, Thomas, another James, Thaddaeus, Simon the Zealot, and Judas Iscariot, who later betrayed Him."},{"sc":"mountside","n":"🔎 Did you know? What a mixed team! Fishermen and a tax collector. Simon 'the Zealot' probably belonged to a group that wanted to fight the Romans, and Matthew had worked FOR the Romans! Jesus brought enemies together into one team."},{"sc":"mountside","w":"bjesus","e":"smile","t":"Come, be with Me. Then I will send you out."}],"lesson":{"title":"First 'with Him', then 'sent out'","text":"Jesus' first reason for choosing the twelve was 'that they might be with Him'. Only then would He send them out. Being with Jesus comes before working for Jesus. And He chose a very mixed team. Leaders spend time with Jesus first, and build teams of very different people."},"order":["Jesus goes up a mountainside","He calls those He wants","He appoints twelve","First to be with Him","Then to be sent out","A very mixed team"],"quiz":[{"q":"What was the first reason Jesus chose the twelve?","o":["That they might be with Him","To fight","To get rich","To build a temple"],"why":"Mark 3:14."},{"q":"What nickname did Jesus give James and John?","o":["Sons of Thunder","Sons of Fire","The Rocks","The Fishermen"],"why":"Mark 3:17."},{"q":"Which disciple later betrayed Jesus?","o":["Judas Iscariot","Thomas","Peter","Andrew"],"why":"Mark 3:19."}],"words":["TWELVE","THUNDER","TEAM","CHOSEN","WITH","SENT"]},"mk6":{"passage":[[4,35,41]],"intro":[{"sc":"galilee","n":"That evening, Jesus said to His disciples, \"Let's go over to the other side of the lake.\" So they set off in the boat."},{"sc":"nightsea","n":"A furious squall came up. Waves broke over the boat, so that it was nearly swamped."},{"sc":"nightsea","n":"And Jesus? He was in the back of the boat, sleeping on a cushion!"},{"sc":"nightsea","w":"bpeter","e":"shock","t":"Teacher, don't You care if we drown?!"},{"sc":"nightsea","n":"Jesus got up, spoke firmly to the wind, and said to the waves:"},{"sc":"nightsea","w":"bjesus","e":"stern","t":"Quiet! Be still!"},{"sc":"galilee","n":"The wind died down, and it was completely calm. \"Why are you so afraid? Do you still have no faith?\" The disciples were terrified and asked each other, \"Who is this? Even the wind and the waves obey Him!\""},{"sc":"nightsea","n":"🔎 Did you know? Only Mark mentions the cushion! That's the kind of detail an eyewitness like Peter would remember."}],"lesson":{"title":"Jesus is in your boat","text":"The disciples were professional fishermen, and they were terrified. Jesus slept peacefully, then calmed the storm with three words. The storm didn't mean Jesus didn't care; He was right there in the boat. When storms come, remember who is in the boat with you."},"order":["They set off across the lake","A furious storm hits","Jesus sleeps on a cushion","\"Don't You care if we drown?\"","\"Quiet! Be still!\"","\"Who is this? Even the wind obeys Him!\""],"quiz":[{"q":"What was Jesus doing in the storm?","o":["Sleeping on a cushion","Rowing","Fishing","Praying loudly"],"why":"Mark 4:38."},{"q":"What did Jesus say to the waves?","o":["Quiet! Be still!","Go away!","Stop it!","Help!"],"why":"Mark 4:39."},{"q":"What did the disciples ask afterwards?","o":["Who is this? Even the wind and waves obey Him!","Can we go home?","Where is the food?","Nothing"],"why":"Mark 4:41."}],"words":["STORM","STILL","CUSHION","WAVES","CALM","OBEY"]},"mk7":{"passage":[[5,1,20]],"intro":[{"sc":"gerasa","n":"On the other side of the lake, in the region of the Gerasenes, a man came out of the tombs to meet Jesus. He was tormented by many evil spirits."},{"sc":"gerasa","n":"Nobody could control him, not even with chains. Night and day he cried out among the tombs and in the hills, and cut himself with stones. Everyone was afraid of him."},{"sc":"gerasa","n":"When he saw Jesus from a distance, he ran and fell on his knees. Jesus asked, \"What is your name?\" \"My name is Legion, for we are many.\""},{"sc":"gerasa","n":"The spirits begged to be sent into a large herd of pigs feeding on the hillside. Jesus gave them permission, and the herd, about two thousand pigs, rushed down the steep bank into the lake!"},{"sc":"gerasa","n":"When the townspeople came, they found the man sitting there, dressed and in his right mind. But they were afraid, and begged Jesus to leave."},{"sc":"galilee","w":"bjesus","e":"smile","t":"Go home to your own people and tell them how much the Lord has done for you, and how He has had mercy on you."},{"sc":"galilee","n":"So the man went and told the whole region of the Decapolis, ten towns, what Jesus had done for him. And all the people were amazed."}],"lesson":{"title":"No one is beyond Jesus' help","text":"Everyone had given up on this man: chained, alone, living among graves. Jesus crossed a stormy lake just to set him free. And then He sent him home to tell his story. Your story of what God has done for you is powerful. Leaders share it, starting at home."},"order":["A man lives among the tombs","No chains can hold him","He falls at Jesus' feet","Jesus sends the spirits into pigs","The man is calm and in his right mind","He tells ten towns what Jesus did"],"quiz":[{"q":"Where did the man live?","o":["Among the tombs","In a palace","In the temple","On a boat"],"why":"Mark 5:3."},{"q":"Where did the herd of pigs go?","o":["Down the bank into the lake","Into the hills","Home","Nowhere"],"why":"Mark 5:13."},{"q":"What did Jesus tell the man to do?","o":["Go home and tell what the Lord did for him","Follow Him in the boat","Hide","Say nothing"],"why":"Mark 5:19."}],"words":["TOMBS","CHAINS","LEGION","PIGS","FREE","TELL"]},"mk8":{"passage":[[5,24,34]],"intro":[{"sc":"market","n":"A large crowd followed Jesus, pressing around Him on every side."},{"sc":"market","n":"In the crowd was a woman who had been bleeding for twelve years. She had suffered a great deal under many doctors and spent all her money, but instead of getting better, she got worse. Her illness also meant she was considered 'unclean', and left out."},{"sc":"market","w":"bwomancloak","e":"worried","t":"If I just touch His clothes, I will be healed."},{"sc":"market","n":"She came up behind Jesus in the crowd and touched His cloak. Immediately her bleeding stopped, and she felt in her body that she was healed!"},{"sc":"market","w":"bjesus","e":"stern","t":"Who touched My clothes?"},{"sc":"market","w":"bpeter","e":"shock","t":"You see the crowd pushing against You, and You ask, 'Who touched Me?'"},{"sc":"market","n":"But Jesus kept looking around. The woman, trembling with fear, came and fell at His feet and told Him the whole truth."},{"sc":"market","w":"bjesus","e":"smile","t":"Daughter, your faith has healed you. Go in peace, and be freed from your suffering."}],"lesson":{"title":"You're not just a face in the crowd","text":"Hundreds of people were pushing against Jesus, but He noticed one hidden, trembling woman, and stopped everything for her. He didn't just heal her body; He called her 'Daughter' in front of everyone, giving her back her dignity. Leaders notice individuals, not just crowds."},"order":["A large crowd presses around Jesus","A woman has been ill for twelve years","She touches His cloak","She is healed immediately","\"Who touched My clothes?\"","\"Daughter, your faith has healed you\""],"quiz":[{"q":"How long had the woman been ill?","o":["Twelve years","Two days","Forty years","One year"],"why":"Mark 5:25."},{"q":"What did she touch?","o":["Jesus' cloak","His hand","His feet","His head"],"why":"Mark 5:27."},{"q":"What did Jesus call her?","o":["Daughter","Woman","Stranger","Sister"],"why":"Mark 5:34."}],"words":["CLOAK","TOUCH","CROWD","DAUGHTER","PEACE","FAITH"]},"mk9":{"passage":[[5,21,24],[5,35,43]],"intro":[{"sc":"galilee","n":"When Jesus crossed back over the lake, a synagogue leader named Jairus came and fell at His feet."},{"sc":"galilee","w":"bjairus","e":"worried","t":"My little daughter is dying. Please come and put Your hands on her so that she will be healed and live!"},{"sc":"market","n":"Jesus went with him. But on the way, Jesus stopped for the woman who touched His cloak. And while He was still speaking, people came from Jairus's house: \"Your daughter is dead. Why bother the teacher any more?\""},{"sc":"market","w":"bjesus","e":"smile","t":"Don't be afraid; just believe."},{"sc":"upperroom","n":"At the house there was loud crying and wailing. \"Why all this commotion? The child is not dead but asleep.\" They laughed at Him. He put them all out, and took only the girl's father and mother and Peter, James and John into the room."},{"sc":"upperroom","w":"bjesus","e":"smile","t":"Talitha koum! (Little girl, I say to you, get up!)"},{"sc":"upperroom","n":"Immediately the girl, who was twelve years old, stood up and began to walk around! Everyone was completely astonished. And Jesus told them to give her something to eat."},{"sc":"upperroom","n":"🔎 Did you know? 'Talitha koum' is Aramaic, the everyday language Jesus spoke. Mark kept His exact words, as Peter remembered them. Notice Jesus' practical kindness too: 'Give her something to eat!'"}],"lesson":{"title":"Don't be afraid; just believe","text":"When the terrible news came, Jesus spoke straight to Jairus: 'Don't be afraid; just believe.' And He was kind and gentle: He took the little girl by the hand, spoke to her in her own language, and remembered she'd be hungry. Leaders hold on to faith when news is bad, and care about the small practical things."},"order":["Jairus begs Jesus to come","Jesus stops for the woman on the way","News comes: \"Your daughter is dead\"","\"Don't be afraid; just believe\"","\"Talitha koum!\"","The girl gets up and walks"],"quiz":[{"q":"How old was Jairus's daughter?","o":["Twelve","Five","Twenty","Three"],"why":"Mark 5:42."},{"q":"What does 'Talitha koum' mean?","o":["Little girl, get up!","Go to sleep","Be quiet","Hello"],"why":"Mark 5:41."},{"q":"What did Jesus tell them to give her?","o":["Something to eat","New clothes","Money","A bath"],"why":"Mark 5:43."}],"words":["JAIRUS","TALITHA","KOUM","BELIEVE","AFRAID","GETUP"]},"mk10":{"passage":[[6,1,6]],"intro":[{"sc":"synagogue","n":"Jesus went back to His home town, Nazareth, with His disciples. On the Sabbath He began to teach in the synagogue."},{"sc":"synagogue","n":"Many who heard Him were amazed. \"Where did this man get these things? What's this wisdom? What are these miracles?\""},{"sc":"synagogue","n":"But then they said: \"Isn't this the carpenter? Isn't this Mary's son, the brother of James, Joseph, Judas and Simon? Aren't His sisters here with us?\" And they took offence at Him."},{"sc":"synagogue","w":"bjesus","e":"smile","t":"A prophet is not without honour, except in his own town, among his relatives and in his own home."},{"sc":"synagogue","n":"He could not do many miracles there, except lay His hands on a few sick people and heal them. And He was amazed at their lack of faith."},{"sc":"synagogue","n":"🔎 Did you know? The word for 'carpenter' can also mean a builder who works with wood and stone. Jesus spent most of His life working with His hands, until He was about thirty!"}],"lesson":{"title":"Don't let familiarity blind you","text":"The people of Nazareth thought they knew all about Jesus: 'just the carpenter'. Their familiarity made them miss who He really was. Sometimes people who know us best find it hardest to see what God is doing in us. Leaders don't give up when home is the hardest place."},"order":["Jesus teaches in Nazareth","People are amazed","\"Isn't this the carpenter?\"","They take offence","\"A prophet has no honour at home\"","He's amazed at their lack of faith"],"quiz":[{"q":"What job did the people of Nazareth know Jesus by?","o":["Carpenter","Fisherman","Shepherd","Tax collector"],"why":"Mark 6:3."},{"q":"What amazed Jesus in Nazareth?","o":["Their lack of faith","Their kindness","Their food","Their synagogue"],"why":"Mark 6:6."},{"q":"Where is a prophet without honour?","o":["In his own town and home","Everywhere","In the temple","In Rome"],"why":"Mark 6:4."}],"words":["NAZARETH","CARPENTER","HONOUR","HOME","FAITH","OFFENCE"]},"mk11":{"passage":[[6,17,29]],"intro":[{"sc":"prison","n":"King Herod Antipas (the son of the Herod who tried to kill baby Jesus) had arrested John the Baptist and put him in prison. John had told him, \"It's not right for you to marry your brother's wife.\""},{"sc":"prison","n":"Herodias, the wife, hated John and wanted him dead. But Herod was afraid of John, knowing he was a righteous and holy man. He liked to listen to John, even though it puzzled him."},{"sc":"banquet","n":"On Herod's birthday, he threw a banquet for his officials. Herodias's daughter danced, and Herod was so pleased that he made a foolish promise in front of everyone: \"Ask me for anything you want, up to half my kingdom!\""},{"sc":"banquet","n":"The girl asked her mother, who told her to ask for John the Baptist's death. The king was very sad, but because of his promise in front of his guests, he didn't want to refuse."},{"sc":"prison","n":"So John was executed in the prison. His disciples came, took his body and laid it in a tomb. Then they went and told Jesus."},{"sc":"prison","n":"🔎 Did you know? Jesus said of John: 'Among those born of women, there has not risen anyone greater than John the Baptist' (Matthew 11:11). John told the truth to the most powerful man around him, and it cost him his life."}],"lesson":{"title":"Telling the truth takes courage","text":"John told a king the truth, knowing it could cost him everything. Herod, on the other hand, cared more about looking good in front of his guests than doing what was right. Leaders speak truth bravely, and never let pride keep them from doing right."},"order":["John tells Herod the truth","Herod puts him in prison","Herodias hates John","Herod makes a foolish promise at his party","Herodias asks for John's death","John's disciples bury him and tell Jesus"],"quiz":[{"q":"Why was John put in prison?","o":["He told Herod the truth about his marriage","He stole","He fought","He lied"],"why":"Mark 6:18."},{"q":"Why did Herod not refuse the request?","o":["He'd promised in front of his guests","He wanted to","He forgot","He was asleep"],"why":"Mark 6:26."},{"q":"Who did John's disciples tell?","o":["Jesus","Pilate","The high priest","Nobody"],"why":"Matthew 14:12."}],"words":["JOHN","TRUTH","COURAGE","PRISON","HEROD","PROMISE"]},"mk12":{"passage":[[6,30,44]],"intro":[{"sc":"galilee","n":"The disciples came back from their mission, full of stories. So many people were coming and going that they didn't even have time to eat! Jesus said, \"Come with Me to a quiet place and get some rest.\""},{"sc":"mountside","n":"But the crowds ran ahead and got there first! When Jesus saw the large crowd, He had compassion on them, because they were like sheep without a shepherd. So He began teaching them many things."},{"sc":"mountside","w":"bpeter","e":"worried","t":"It's getting late. Send the people away so they can buy themselves something to eat."},{"sc":"mountside","w":"bjesus","e":"smile","t":"You give them something to eat."},{"sc":"mountside","n":"\"That would take more than half a year's wages!\" \"How many loaves do you have? Go and see.\" They found out: \"Five, and two fish.\" (John's Gospel tells us they came from a boy's lunch!)"},{"sc":"mountside","n":"Jesus had everyone sit down in groups of hundreds and fifties on the green grass. He took the five loaves and two fish, looked up to heaven, gave thanks, and broke the loaves. He kept giving them to the disciples to hand out."},{"sc":"mountside","n":"They all ate and were satisfied! And the disciples picked up twelve basketfuls of leftover bread and fish. The number of men who had eaten was five thousand, plus women and children!"}],"lesson":{"title":"Bring what you have","text":"Five loaves and two fish for thousands of people: impossible! But Jesus took what was offered, gave thanks, and there was more than enough, with twelve baskets left over. Don't think what you have is too small. Bring it to Jesus. Leaders give thanks for what they have, and trust God to multiply it."},"order":["Jesus has compassion on the crowd","The disciples say, \"Send them away\"","\"You give them something to eat\"","Five loaves and two fish","Jesus gives thanks and breaks the bread","Everyone eats; twelve baskets are left"],"quiz":[{"q":"How many loaves and fish were there?","o":["Five loaves and two fish","Two loaves and five fish","Twelve loaves","One fish"],"why":"Mark 6:38."},{"q":"How many baskets of leftovers?","o":["Twelve","Five","Two","None"],"why":"Mark 6:43."},{"q":"What were the crowds like, according to Jesus?","o":["Sheep without a shepherd","Lions","Birds","Soldiers"],"why":"Mark 6:34."}],"words":["LOAVES","FISH","FIVE","THOUSAND","BASKETS","THANKS"]},"mk13":{"passage":[[7,24,30]],"intro":[{"sc":"hut","n":"Jesus went north to the region of Tyre, outside Israel, and tried to stay hidden in a house. But He couldn't keep His presence secret."},{"sc":"hut","n":"A woman whose little daughter was troubled by an evil spirit heard about Him and came and fell at His feet. She was a Greek, born in Syrian Phoenicia: not Jewish. She begged Jesus to drive the spirit out of her daughter."},{"sc":"hut","w":"bjesus","e":"smile","t":"First let the children eat all they want. It isn't right to take the children's bread and toss it to the little dogs."},{"sc":"hut","n":"Jesus' mission was first to the people of Israel. But He was testing her, and drawing out her faith."},{"sc":"hut","w":"bsyromum","e":"smile","t":"Lord, even the little dogs under the table eat the children's crumbs!"},{"sc":"hut","w":"bjesus","e":"big","t":"For such a reply, you may go. The demon has left your daughter."},{"sc":"hut","n":"She went home and found her child lying on the bed, and the demon gone."}],"lesson":{"title":"Persistent, humble faith","text":"This foreign mother wouldn't give up. She didn't argue that she deserved help. She simply believed that even a crumb from Jesus would be enough. Jesus loved her answer! Leaders keep asking God with humble, persistent faith, and know that His grace is for every nation."},"order":["Jesus goes to the region of Tyre","A foreign mother falls at His feet","She begs Him to heal her daughter","Jesus tests her faith","\"Even the dogs eat the crumbs\"","Her daughter is healed"],"quiz":[{"q":"Where was the mother from?","o":["Syrian Phoenicia, near Tyre","Jerusalem","Egypt","Rome"],"why":"Mark 7:26."},{"q":"What did the mother say even the little dogs eat?","o":["The children's crumbs","Meat","Nothing","Bones"],"why":"Mark 7:28."},{"q":"What happened to her daughter?","o":["She was healed","Nothing","She ran away","She was sick for longer"],"why":"Mark 7:30."}],"words":["CRUMBS","MOTHER","TYRE","FAITH","PERSIST","HUMBLE"]},"mk14":{"passage":[[7,31,37]],"intro":[{"sc":"hillcountry","n":"Some people brought to Jesus a man who was deaf and could hardly talk, and begged Him to place His hand on him."},{"sc":"hillcountry","n":"Jesus took him aside, away from the crowd, so it was just the two of them."},{"sc":"hillcountry","n":"Jesus put His fingers into the man's ears. Then He spat and touched the man's tongue. It was a kind of sign language, so the deaf man could understand what Jesus was about to do!"},{"sc":"hillcountry","w":"bjesus","e":"smile","t":"Ephphatha! (Be opened!)"},{"sc":"hillcountry","n":"Jesus looked up to heaven, and with a deep sigh, said it. At this, the man's ears were opened, his tongue was loosened, and he began to speak plainly!"},{"sc":"hillcountry","n":"The people were overwhelmed with amazement. \"He has done everything well! He even makes the deaf hear and the mute speak!\""},{"sc":"hillcountry","n":"📜 Promise kept: Isaiah had promised: 'Then the eyes of the blind will be opened, and the ears of the deaf unstopped... and the mute tongue will shout for joy' (Isaiah 35:5-6). Jesus was showing that God's promised kingdom had arrived!"}],"lesson":{"title":"Jesus meets each person where they are","text":"Jesus took the deaf man away from the noisy crowd, and 'spoke' to him in a way he could understand: with touch and signs. He cared about how this one man would experience the miracle. Leaders find ways to communicate that each person can understand."},"order":["A deaf man is brought to Jesus","Jesus takes him away from the crowd","Jesus touches his ears and tongue","\"Ephphatha! Be opened!\"","The man hears and speaks plainly","\"He has done everything well!\""],"quiz":[{"q":"What does 'Ephphatha' mean?","o":["Be opened!","Get up!","Be quiet!","Go home!"],"why":"Mark 7:34."},{"q":"Why did Jesus take the man away from the crowd?","o":["To be alone with him","To hide","To rest","To eat"],"why":"Mark 7:33."},{"q":"What did the people say?","o":["\"He has done everything well!\"","\"Go away!\"","\"That's strange\"","Nothing"],"why":"Mark 7:37."}],"words":["EPHPHATHA","OPENED","DEAF","SPEAK","EARS","WELL"]},"mk15":{"passage":[[9,33,37],[10,13,16]],"intro":[{"sc":"hillcountry","n":"On the road, the disciples argued about something. When they got to the house, Jesus asked, \"What were you arguing about?\" They kept quiet, because they'd been arguing about who was the greatest!"},{"sc":"hut","w":"bjesus","e":"smile","t":"Anyone who wants to be first must be the very last, and the servant of all."},{"sc":"hut","n":"He took a little child and had them stand among them. Then He took the child in His arms. \"Whoever welcomes one of these little children in My name welcomes Me.\""},{"sc":"hillcountry","n":"Another day, people were bringing little children to Jesus for Him to place His hands on them. But the disciples told them off, thinking Jesus was too busy and important for children."},{"sc":"hillcountry","w":"bjesus","e":"stern","t":"Let the little children come to Me, and don't stop them, for the kingdom of God belongs to such as these!"},{"sc":"hillcountry","n":"And He took the children in His arms, placed His hands on them and blessed them."},{"sc":"hillcountry","n":"🔎 Did you know? Mark tells us Jesus was 'indignant', really annoyed, when the disciples sent the children away. In those days, children were often seen as unimportant. Jesus thought they were very important!"}],"lesson":{"title":"You matter to Jesus","text":"The disciples thought Jesus was too busy for children. Jesus was annoyed, and said: let them come! He took them in His arms and blessed them. You are never too young to come to Jesus, and He is never too busy for you. And true greatness means serving others, not being first."},"order":["The disciples argue about who is greatest","\"The first must be last\"","Jesus takes a child in His arms","People bring children to Jesus","The disciples send them away","\"Let the little children come to Me\""],"quiz":[{"q":"What were the disciples arguing about?","o":["Who was the greatest","Food","The weather","Money"],"why":"Mark 9:34."},{"q":"How did Jesus feel when children were sent away?","o":["Indignant, really annoyed","Pleased","Tired","Relieved"],"why":"Mark 10:14."},{"q":"Who does the kingdom of God belong to?","o":["Such as these little children","Only adults","Only priests","Only kings"],"why":"Mark 10:14."}],"words":["CHILDREN","COME","BLESSED","GREATEST","SERVANT","ARMS"]},"mk16":{"passage":[[10,17,27]],"intro":[{"sc":"market","n":"As Jesus started on His way, a man ran up and fell on his knees before Him."},{"sc":"market","w":"brichman","e":"worried","t":"Good teacher, what must I do to inherit eternal life?"},{"sc":"market","w":"bjesus","e":"smile","t":"You know the commandments: don't murder, don't steal, don't lie, honour your father and mother..."},{"sc":"market","w":"brichman","e":"smile","t":"Teacher, all these I have kept since I was a boy."},{"sc":"market","n":"Jesus looked at him and loved him."},{"sc":"market","w":"bjesus","e":"smile","t":"One thing you lack. Go, sell everything you have and give to the poor, and you will have treasure in heaven. Then come, follow Me."},{"sc":"market","n":"At this the man's face fell. He went away sad, because he had great wealth."},{"sc":"market","w":"bjesus","e":"smile","t":"It is easier for a camel to go through the eye of a needle than for someone who is rich to enter the kingdom of God. With people this is impossible, but not with God; all things are possible with God."}],"lesson":{"title":"What do you love most?","text":"The young man was good and keen. Jesus loved him. But his money had his heart, and he couldn't let it go to follow Jesus. Jesus doesn't ask everyone to sell everything, but He asks everyone: am I first in your life? Leaders hold their possessions loosely and put Jesus first."},"order":["A rich young man runs up to Jesus","\"What must I do for eternal life?\"","He has kept the commandments","Jesus looks at him and loves him","\"Sell everything and follow Me\"","He goes away sad"],"quiz":[{"q":"What did Jesus feel when He looked at the young man?","o":["Love","Anger","Boredom","Disgust"],"why":"Mark 10:21."},{"q":"Why did the man go away sad?","o":["He had great wealth","He was tired","He was sick","He was lost"],"why":"Mark 10:22."},{"q":"What did Jesus say about a camel?","o":["It's easier for it to go through the eye of a needle","It's slow","It's tall","It can swim"],"why":"Mark 10:25."}],"words":["RICH","CAMEL","NEEDLE","TREASURE","FOLLOW","POSSIBLE"]},"mk17":{"passage":[[10,35,45]],"intro":[{"sc":"hillcountry","w":"bjames","e":"smile","t":"Teacher, we want You to do for us whatever we ask."},{"sc":"hillcountry","w":"bjesus","e":"smile","t":"What do you want Me to do for you?"},{"sc":"hillcountry","w":"bjohnapos","e":"smile","t":"Let one of us sit at Your right and the other at Your left in Your glory!"},{"sc":"hillcountry","n":"James and John wanted the top two seats in Jesus' kingdom! When the other ten heard, they were angry with them."},{"sc":"hillcountry","w":"bjesus","e":"smile","t":"You know that the rulers of the world lord it over their people, and their high officials boss them around. Not so with you!"},{"sc":"hillcountry","w":"bjesus","e":"big","t":"Whoever wants to become great among you must be your servant, and whoever wants to be first must be slave of all. For even the Son of Man did not come to be served, but to serve, and to give His life as a ransom for many."}],"lesson":{"title":"Real leaders serve","text":"James and John wanted power and status. Jesus turned leadership upside down: the greatest are the ones who serve. And He's the example: the King of the universe came to serve and to give His life. This is the most important leadership lesson in the whole game."},"order":["James and John ask for a favour","They want the top seats in glory","The other disciples are angry","\"The world's rulers boss people around\"","\"Not so with you!\"","\"The Son of Man came to serve\""],"quiz":[{"q":"What did James and John ask for?","o":["The seats at Jesus' right and left","Money","Food","A boat"],"why":"Mark 10:37."},{"q":"According to Jesus, who is great?","o":["The one who serves","The one who is rich","The one who bosses others","The tallest"],"why":"Mark 10:43."},{"q":"What did Jesus say He came to do?","o":["Serve, and give His life as a ransom","Be served","Rule Rome","Get rich"],"why":"Mark 10:45."}],"words":["SERVE","SERVANT","GREAT","RANSOM","FIRST","LEADER"]},"mk18":{"passage":[[10,46,52]],"intro":[{"sc":"citygate","n":"As Jesus and His disciples, with a large crowd, were leaving Jericho, a blind man named Bartimaeus was sitting by the roadside, begging."},{"sc":"citygate","n":"When he heard that it was Jesus of Nazareth, he began to shout:"},{"sc":"citygate","w":"bbartimaeus","e":"worried","t":"Jesus, Son of David, have mercy on me!"},{"sc":"citygate","n":"Many people told him off and told him to be quiet. But he shouted all the more: \"Son of David, have mercy on me!\""},{"sc":"citygate","n":"Jesus stopped. \"Call him.\" So they called to the blind man: \"Cheer up! On your feet! He's calling you!\" Throwing his cloak aside, he jumped to his feet and came to Jesus."},{"sc":"citygate","w":"bjesus","e":"smile","t":"What do you want Me to do for you?"},{"sc":"citygate","w":"bbartimaeus","e":"worried","t":"Rabbi, I want to see."},{"sc":"citygate","w":"bjesus","e":"smile","t":"Go, your faith has healed you."},{"sc":"citygate","n":"Immediately he received his sight, and followed Jesus along the road."}],"lesson":{"title":"Don't let anyone silence your prayer","text":"The crowd told Bartimaeus to be quiet. He shouted louder. He threw off his cloak, probably his most valuable possession as a beggar, and ran to Jesus. And when he could see, he followed. Leaders don't let others silence their cry to God, and they follow Jesus once they've met Him."},"order":["Bartimaeus sits by the road begging","He shouts, \"Son of David, have mercy!\"","People tell him to be quiet","He shouts even louder","He throws off his cloak","He receives his sight and follows Jesus"],"quiz":[{"q":"What did Bartimaeus do when told to be quiet?","o":["Shouted even louder","Stopped","Went home","Cried"],"why":"Mark 10:48."},{"q":"What did he throw aside?","o":["His cloak","His stick","His bowl","His shoes"],"why":"Mark 10:50."},{"q":"What did he do after he could see?","o":["Followed Jesus along the road","Went home","Sat down again","Bought a cloak"],"why":"Mark 10:52."}],"words":["BARTIMAEUS","BLIND","SHOUT","MERCY","CLOAK","SIGHT"]},"mk19":{"passage":[[11,7,11],[11,15,18]],"intro":[{"sc":"donkeyking","n":"As they came near Jerusalem, Jesus sent two disciples to bring a young donkey that no one had ever ridden. They threw their cloaks over it, and Jesus sat on it."},{"sc":"donkeyking","n":"Many people spread their cloaks on the road, and others spread branches they had cut in the fields. Those who went ahead and those who followed shouted: \"Hosanna! Blessed is He who comes in the name of the Lord! Blessed is the coming kingdom of our father David!\""},{"sc":"temple","n":"The next day, Jesus went into the temple courts. The outer court, the only place where non-Jewish people could pray, was full of noisy stalls, money changers and people selling doves, often cheating poor worshippers."},{"sc":"temple","n":"Jesus began driving out those who were buying and selling. He overturned the tables of the money changers and the benches of those selling doves."},{"sc":"temple","w":"bjesus","e":"stern","t":"Isn't it written: 'My house will be called a house of prayer for all nations'? But you have made it a den of robbers!"},{"sc":"donkeyking","n":"📜 Promise kept: Zechariah had promised: 'See, your King comes to you, lowly and riding on a donkey' (Zechariah 9:9). And Jesus quoted Isaiah 56:7: 'a house of prayer for all nations'. God's house was meant to welcome every nation, and the market was crowding them out."}],"lesson":{"title":"Make room for everyone","text":"Jesus rode in humbly on a donkey, then acted with strong anger against people who turned God's house into a cheating market, and crowded out the nations who came to pray. Leaders are gentle and humble, but they also stand up firmly against injustice."},"order":["Jesus rides a young donkey","The crowd spreads cloaks and branches","\"Hosanna!\"","The temple courts are full of sellers","Jesus overturns the tables","\"A house of prayer for all nations\""],"quiz":[{"q":"What did the crowd shout?","o":["Hosanna!","Crucify!","Go home!","Nothing"],"why":"Mark 11:9."},{"q":"What did Jesus overturn in the temple?","o":["The money changers' tables","The altar","The lampstand","Nothing"],"why":"Mark 11:15."},{"q":"What did Jesus say God's house should be?","o":["A house of prayer for all nations","A market","A palace","A bank"],"why":"Mark 11:17."}],"words":["HOSANNA","DONKEY","TEMPLE","TABLES","PRAYER","NATIONS"]},"mk20":{"passage":[[12,41,44]],"intro":[{"sc":"temple","n":"Jesus sat down opposite the place where the offerings were put, and watched the crowd putting their money into the temple treasury."},{"sc":"temple","n":"Many rich people threw in large amounts. You could hear the clinking and clanging of their coins!"},{"sc":"temple","n":"But a poor widow came and put in two very small copper coins, worth only a fraction of a penny. Barely a sound."},{"sc":"temple","w":"bjesus","e":"smile","t":"Truly I tell you, this poor widow has put more into the treasury than all the others."},{"sc":"temple","w":"bjesus","e":"smile","t":"They all gave out of their wealth. But she, out of her poverty, put in everything, all she had to live on."},{"sc":"temple","n":"🔎 Did you know? The widow's coins were called 'lepta', the smallest coins in use, worth about 1/64 of a day's wage. But Jesus doesn't measure gifts by their size. He measures them by the heart, and by what they cost the giver."}],"lesson":{"title":"God sees the heart","text":"Nobody else noticed the widow's tiny gift. Jesus did, and said she gave more than all the rich people put together. God doesn't measure how big your gift is, but how big your heart is. Leaders give generously, even when it's small, and notice the quiet givers."},"order":["Jesus watches people giving","Rich people give large amounts","A poor widow gives two tiny coins","\"She has given more than all the others\"","They gave from their wealth","She gave all she had"],"quiz":[{"q":"How many coins did the widow give?","o":["Two small copper coins","Twelve gold coins","One silver coin","Nothing"],"why":"Mark 12:42."},{"q":"Who did Jesus say gave the most?","o":["The poor widow","The richest man","The priests","Nobody"],"why":"Mark 12:43."},{"q":"Why did she give the most?","o":["She gave all she had to live on","Her coins were gold","She was rich","She gave loudly"],"why":"Mark 12:44."}],"words":["WIDOW","COINS","GIVE","HEART","POOR","GENEROUS"]},"mk21":{"passage":[[14,3,9]],"intro":[{"sc":"banquet","n":"A few days before Passover, Jesus was in Bethany, reclining at dinner. A woman came with an alabaster jar of very expensive perfume, made of pure nard."},{"sc":"banquet","n":"She broke the jar and poured the perfume on Jesus' head. The whole house filled with the beautiful smell. (John tells us her name: Mary, the sister of Martha and Lazarus.)"},{"sc":"banquet","n":"Some of those present were angry: \"Why this waste of perfume? It could have been sold for more than a year's wages and the money given to the poor!\" And they scolded her harshly."},{"sc":"banquet","w":"bjesus","e":"stern","t":"Leave her alone. Why are you bothering her? She has done a beautiful thing to Me."},{"sc":"banquet","w":"bjesus","e":"smile","t":"You will always have the poor with you, and you can help them any time you want. But you will not always have Me. She poured perfume on My body beforehand to prepare for My burial."},{"sc":"banquet","w":"bjesus","e":"big","t":"Truly I tell you, wherever the gospel is preached throughout the world, what she has done will also be told, in memory of her."}],"lesson":{"title":"Extravagant love for Jesus","text":"Others called it a waste. Jesus called it 'a beautiful thing'. She gave her most precious possession, out of love, at just the right time, as if she understood He was going to die. And Jesus' promise came true: we're telling her story right now! Leaders love Jesus wholeheartedly, even if others don't understand."},"order":["Jesus is at dinner in Bethany","A woman breaks a jar of perfume","She pours it on Jesus' head","Some call it a waste","\"She has done a beautiful thing\"","\"Her story will be told everywhere\""],"quiz":[{"q":"What was the jar made of?","o":["Alabaster","Clay","Gold","Glass"],"why":"Mark 14:3."},{"q":"What did Jesus call what she did?","o":["A beautiful thing","A waste","Silly","Wrong"],"why":"Mark 14:6."},{"q":"What did Jesus say would happen to her story?","o":["It would be told wherever the gospel is preached","It would be forgotten","It would be secret","Nothing"],"why":"Mark 14:9."}],"words":["PERFUME","ALABASTER","BEAUTIFUL","POURED","BETHANY","LOVE"]},"mk22":{"passage":[[14,12,26]],"intro":[{"sc":"lastsupper","n":"On the first day of the Feast of Unleavened Bread, when the Passover lamb was sacrificed, Jesus' disciples prepared the Passover meal in a large upstairs room in Jerusalem."},{"sc":"lastsupper","n":"In the evening, Jesus arrived with the twelve. While they were eating, He said: \"Truly I tell you, one of you will betray Me, one who is eating with Me.\" They were saddened, and one by one asked, \"Surely you don't mean me?\""},{"sc":"lastsupper","w":"bjesus","e":"smile","t":"Take it; this is My body."},{"sc":"lastsupper","n":"Jesus took bread, gave thanks, broke it and gave it to His disciples. Then He took a cup, gave thanks and offered it to them, and they all drank from it."},{"sc":"lastsupper","w":"bjesus","e":"smile","t":"This is My blood of the covenant, which is poured out for many."},{"sc":"lastsupper","n":"When they had sung a hymn, they went out to the Mount of Olives."},{"sc":"lastsupper","n":"📜 Promise kept: This was the Passover meal, remembering the lamb whose blood saved Israel in Egypt. Now Jesus said the bread and cup were about HIM: He is the true Passover Lamb. And 'the covenant' points to Jeremiah's New Covenant (Jeremiah 31:31). Christians still share this meal, called Communion or the Lord's Supper."}],"lesson":{"title":"Remember Him","text":"At the Passover meal, Jesus gave the bread and cup new meaning: His body broken and His blood poured out for us. Every time Christians share Communion, we remember what He did. Leaders remember the cross, and live thankfully because of it."},"order":["The disciples prepare the Passover","Jesus says one will betray Him","\"Surely not I?\"","Jesus breaks the bread: \"This is My body\"","He shares the cup: \"My blood of the covenant\"","They sing a hymn and go out"],"quiz":[{"q":"Which feast were they celebrating?","o":["Passover","Purim","Christmas","Pentecost"],"why":"Mark 14:12."},{"q":"What did Jesus say the bread was?","o":["His body","Just bread","Manna","A gift"],"why":"Mark 14:22."},{"q":"What did they do just before going out?","o":["Sang a hymn","Went to sleep","Washed dishes","Argued"],"why":"Mark 14:26."}],"words":["PASSOVER","BREAD","CUP","COVENANT","BODY","REMEMBER"]},"mk23":{"passage":[[14,32,50],[14,51,52]],"intro":[{"sc":"gethsemane","n":"They went to an olive grove called Gethsemane. Jesus took Peter, James and John with Him, and He began to be deeply troubled and distressed."},{"sc":"gethsemane","w":"bjesus","e":"worried","t":"My soul is overwhelmed with sorrow, to the point of death. Stay here and keep watch."},{"sc":"gethsemane","n":"Going a little further, He fell to the ground and prayed:"},{"sc":"gethsemane","w":"bjesus","e":"worried","t":"Abba, Father, everything is possible for You. Take this cup from Me. Yet not what I will, but what You will."},{"sc":"gethsemane","n":"He came back and found the disciples asleep. \"Couldn't you keep watch for one hour? Watch and pray so that you will not fall into temptation. The spirit is willing, but the flesh is weak.\" Three times He prayed, and three times they fell asleep."},{"sc":"gethsemane","n":"Then Judas arrived, with a crowd carrying swords and clubs. \"The one I kiss is the man.\" He went up to Jesus: \"Rabbi!\" and kissed Him. They seized Jesus and arrested Him. And all the disciples deserted Him and ran away."},{"sc":"gethsemane","n":"🔎 Did you know? Only Mark mentions a young man who was following Jesus, wearing just a linen cloth. When they grabbed him, he slipped out of it and ran away! Many think this young man was Mark himself, quietly putting himself in the story."}],"lesson":{"title":"Not my will, but Yours","text":"Jesus didn't pretend to be fine. He told His friends He was overwhelmed, and told His Father exactly what He wanted. But He ended: 'not what I will, but what You will.' That's the most powerful prayer anyone can pray. Leaders are honest with God, and surrender to His will."},"order":["Jesus goes to Gethsemane","He is deeply troubled","\"Not what I will, but what You will\"","The disciples fall asleep three times","Judas betrays Jesus with a kiss","The disciples run away"],"quiz":[{"q":"What was the garden called?","o":["Gethsemane","Eden","Bethany","Jericho"],"why":"Mark 14:32."},{"q":"What did Jesus call God in His prayer?","o":["Abba, Father","King","Master","Lord of armies"],"why":"Mark 14:36."},{"q":"How did Judas show the soldiers which one was Jesus?","o":["With a kiss","By pointing","By shouting","With a torch"],"why":"Mark 14:44-45."}],"words":["GARDEN","PRAY","ABBA","WILL","WATCH","KISS"]},"mk24":{"passage":[[14,53,54],[14,61,72]],"intro":[{"sc":"courtyardfire","n":"They took Jesus to the high priest's house. Peter followed at a distance, right into the courtyard, and sat with the guards, warming himself at the fire."},{"sc":"throne","w":"bcaiaphas","e":"stern","t":"Are You the Messiah, the Son of the Blessed One?"},{"sc":"throne","w":"bjesus","e":"stern","t":"I am. And you will see the Son of Man sitting at the right hand of the Mighty One and coming on the clouds of heaven."},{"sc":"throne","n":"The high priest tore his clothes. \"Why do we need any more witnesses?\" They all condemned Him as worthy of death."},{"sc":"courtyardfire","w":"bmaid2","e":"stern","t":"You also were with that Nazarene, Jesus!"},{"sc":"courtyardfire","w":"bpeter","e":"worried","t":"I don't know or understand what you're talking about!"},{"sc":"courtyardfire","n":"A second time, then a third time, people said, \"Surely you are one of them!\" Peter began to call down curses: \"I don't know this man you're talking about!\""},{"sc":"courtyardfire","n":"Immediately the rooster crowed the second time. Then Peter remembered Jesus' words: \"Before the rooster crows twice, you will disown Me three times.\" And he broke down and wept."}],"lesson":{"title":"Even brave people fall, and can be restored","text":"Only hours before, Peter had said he'd die for Jesus. Then, scared, he denied even knowing Him, three times. But Peter's tears showed his heart was broken. And this isn't the end of Peter's story: Jesus would restore him. If you've let Jesus down, His forgiveness is bigger than your failure."},"order":["Jesus is taken to the high priest","Peter warms himself at the fire","Jesus says, \"I am\"","A servant girl recognises Peter","Peter denies Jesus three times","The rooster crows, and Peter weeps"],"quiz":[{"q":"Where was Peter warming himself?","o":["At a fire in the courtyard","In the temple","At home","By the lake"],"why":"Mark 14:54."},{"q":"How many times did Peter deny Jesus?","o":["Three","Once","Seven","Twice"],"why":"Mark 14:72."},{"q":"What did Peter do when he heard the rooster?","o":["Broke down and wept","Laughed","Ran to Jesus","Fell asleep"],"why":"Mark 14:72."}],"words":["ROOSTER","DENIED","FIRE","PETER","WEPT","THREE"]},"mk25":{"passage":[[15,15,22]],"intro":[{"sc":"throne","n":"In the morning, the leaders handed Jesus over to Pilate, the Roman governor. Although Pilate could find no crime, he gave in to the shouting crowd, had Jesus whipped, and handed Him over to be crucified."},{"sc":"throne","n":"The soldiers mocked Jesus. They dressed Him in a purple robe, twisted a crown of thorns and put it on His head, and called out, \"Hail, king of the Jews!\""},{"sc":"citygate","n":"Then they led Him out to crucify Him. Jesus was too weak from the beating to carry His heavy cross."},{"sc":"citygate","n":"A man named Simon, from Cyrene in North Africa, was passing by on his way in from the country. The soldiers forced him to carry the cross."},{"sc":"citygate","w":"bsimonc","e":"worried","t":"(Simon looks at the wounded man beside him, then lifts the heavy wooden beam onto his own shoulders.)"},{"sc":"citygate","n":"Simon carried the cross behind Jesus, all the way to a place called Golgotha, which means 'the place of the skull'."},{"sc":"citygate","n":"🔎 Did you know? Cyrene was a city in what is now Libya, in Africa! Mark names Simon's sons, Alexander and Rufus, as if his readers knew them. Paul later greets a Christian called Rufus in Rome (Romans 16:13). It seems Simon's whole family became followers of Jesus!"}],"lesson":{"title":"Carry the cross","text":"Simon didn't choose to carry the cross; he was forced. But he ended up walking right behind Jesus, carrying His cross, on the most important day in history. Jesus said, 'Whoever wants to be My disciple must take up their cross and follow Me.' Leaders help carry others' burdens, and follow Jesus even when it's hard."},"order":["Pilate hands Jesus over","Soldiers mock Him with a crown of thorns","Jesus is too weak to carry the cross","Simon of Cyrene is passing by","He is forced to carry the cross","They reach Golgotha"],"quiz":[{"q":"Where was Simon from?","o":["Cyrene, in North Africa","Jerusalem","Rome","Egypt"],"why":"Mark 15:21."},{"q":"What did the soldiers put on Jesus' head?","o":["A crown of thorns","A gold crown","A helmet","A turban"],"why":"Mark 15:17."},{"q":"What were the names of Simon's sons?","o":["Alexander and Rufus","Peter and John","James and Judas","Mark and Luke"],"why":"Mark 15:21."}],"words":["SIMON","CYRENE","AFRICA","CROSS","CARRY","THORNS"]},"mk26":{"passage":[[15,25,39]],"intro":[{"sc":"golgotha","n":"At nine in the morning, they crucified Jesus. The sign above His head read: THE KING OF THE JEWS. Two robbers were crucified with Him, one on His right and one on His left."},{"sc":"golgotha","n":"People passing by shook their heads and mocked Him: \"Come down from the cross and save yourself!\" The chief priests mocked too: \"He saved others, but he can't save himself!\""},{"sc":"golgotha","n":"At noon, darkness came over the whole land until three in the afternoon. At three, Jesus cried out in a loud voice:"},{"sc":"golgotha","w":"bjesus","e":"worried","t":"Eloi, Eloi, lema sabachthani? (My God, My God, why have You forsaken Me?)"},{"sc":"golgotha","n":"With a loud cry, Jesus breathed His last. And at that moment, the curtain of the temple, the huge, thick curtain that separated the Most Holy Place from everyone, was torn in two, from top to bottom!"},{"sc":"golgotha","w":"bcenturion","e":"shock","t":"Surely this man was the Son of God!"},{"sc":"golgotha","n":"📜 Promise kept: Jesus' cry was the first line of Psalm 22, written 1,000 years earlier: the psalm about pierced hands and feet and dice thrown for clothes. And the torn curtain meant the way into God's presence was now open to everyone, through Jesus (Hebrews 10:19-20)."}],"lesson":{"title":"The way is open","text":"Jesus died taking the punishment for our sins, even feeling forsaken by God. And the temple curtain tore from top to bottom: God Himself opened the way for anyone to come to Him. The first person in Mark to say 'He is the Son of God' after His death was a Roman soldier! The cross is for everyone."},"order":["Jesus is crucified at nine","The sign reads: King of the Jews","People mock Him","Darkness covers the land from noon","\"My God, why have You forsaken Me?\"","The temple curtain tears from top to bottom"],"quiz":[{"q":"What was torn in two when Jesus died?","o":["The temple curtain","His clothes","The sign","Nothing"],"why":"Mark 15:38."},{"q":"What did the centurion say?","o":["Surely this man was the Son of God!","Crucify Him!","Go away!","Nothing"],"why":"Mark 15:39."},{"q":"Which psalm begins with 'My God, my God, why have You forsaken me?'","o":["Psalm 22","Psalm 23","Psalm 1","Psalm 150"],"why":"Psalm 22:1."}],"words":["CROSS","CURTAIN","TORN","DARKNESS","FORSAKEN","CENTURION"]},"mk27":{"passage":[[15,40,47]],"intro":[{"sc":"golgotha","n":"Some women were watching from a distance: Mary Magdalene, Mary the mother of James and Joseph, and Salome. They had followed Jesus in Galilee and cared for His needs. When the men ran away, they stayed."},{"sc":"throne","n":"As evening approached, Joseph of Arimathea, a respected member of the Jewish council who was waiting for the kingdom of God, 'took courage' and went to Pilate to ask for Jesus' body."},{"sc":"throne","w":"bjosepharim","e":"worried","t":"Governor, please let me take the body of Jesus, and bury Him."},{"sc":"throne","n":"Pilate was surprised Jesus was already dead. He checked with the centurion, then gave the body to Joseph."},{"sc":"tomb","n":"Joseph bought linen cloth, took down the body, wrapped it in the linen, and placed it in a tomb cut out of rock. Then he rolled a stone against the entrance. Mary Magdalene and Mary the mother of Joseph saw where He was laid."},{"sc":"tomb","n":"📜 Promise kept: Isaiah 53:9 had said the Servant would be 'with the rich in His death'. Joseph of Arimathea was a rich man, and he gave Jesus his own new tomb (Matthew 27:57-60)."}],"lesson":{"title":"Courage at the darkest moment","text":"When Jesus' closest followers had run away, two kinds of courage shone: the women who stayed and watched, and a powerful council member who risked his reputation to give Jesus a proper burial. Leaders show up and do what's right, even when it costs them, even when hope seems lost."},"order":["The women watch from a distance","Joseph of Arimathea takes courage","He asks Pilate for Jesus' body","Pilate agrees","Joseph wraps the body in linen","He lays Jesus in a rock tomb"],"quiz":[{"q":"Who asked Pilate for Jesus' body?","o":["Joseph of Arimathea","Peter","Judas","John the Baptist"],"why":"Mark 15:43."},{"q":"Who stayed watching when the men had run away?","o":["The women who followed Jesus","Nobody","The soldiers only","The priests"],"why":"Mark 15:40-41."},{"q":"What was rolled against the tomb's entrance?","o":["A stone","A door","A cart","A log"],"why":"Mark 15:46."}],"words":["JOSEPH","COURAGE","TOMB","LINEN","STONE","WOMEN"]},"mk28":{"passage":[[16,1,8]],"intro":[{"sc":"tomb","n":"When the Sabbath was over, Mary Magdalene, Mary the mother of James, and Salome bought spices to anoint Jesus' body."},{"sc":"tomb","n":"Very early on the first day of the week, just after sunrise, they were on their way to the tomb, asking each other: \"Who will roll the stone away from the entrance?\" It was very big."},{"sc":"tomb","n":"But when they looked up, they saw that the stone had already been rolled away!"},{"sc":"tomb","n":"Entering the tomb, they saw a young man dressed in a white robe sitting on the right side, and they were alarmed."},{"sc":"tomb","n":"\"Don't be alarmed. You're looking for Jesus the Nazarene, who was crucified. He has risen! He is not here. See the place where they laid Him. But go, tell His disciples AND PETER, 'He is going ahead of you into Galilee. There you will see Him, just as He told you.'\""},{"sc":"tomb","n":"🔎 Did you know? Only Mark includes those two little words: 'and Peter'. Peter had denied Jesus three times. He probably felt he wasn't a disciple any more. But Jesus made sure Peter got a personal invitation! (And remember, Mark probably wrote down Peter's own memories. Peter never forgot those words.)"}],"lesson":{"title":"You're still invited","text":"Peter had failed badly. But the very first message from the empty tomb included his name: 'tell His disciples, and Peter'. If you feel you've failed Jesus too much, hear this: you're still invited. Leaders who've been restored make sure others know they're welcome back too."},"order":["The women buy spices","They wonder who will roll the stone","The stone is already rolled away","A young man in white sits inside","\"He has risen! He is not here\"","\"Tell His disciples, and Peter\""],"quiz":[{"q":"What were the women worried about on the way?","o":["Who would roll the stone away","The rain","The guards' dogs","Getting lost"],"why":"Mark 16:3."},{"q":"Which disciple was named specially in the message?","o":["Peter","John","Judas","Thomas"],"why":"Mark 16:7."},{"q":"Where did the angel say they would see Jesus?","o":["Galilee","Rome","Egypt","Babylon"],"why":"Mark 16:7."}],"words":["RISEN","STONE","WOMEN","SPICES","PETER","INVITED"]}});
